.TH RECO-NOVA 1 "March 2026" "v1.2" "Reco-Nova Manual"
.SH NAME
reco-nova \- Professional Reconnaissance Intelligence Framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reco-nova
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B \-d
\fIDOMAIN\fR
.br
.B reco-nova
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B \-l
\fIFILE\fR
.br
.B reco-nova
.B setup
.br
.B reco-nova
.B monitor
\fIDOMAIN\fR [\fI\-\-interval\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
.br
.B reco-nova
.B report
\fIDOMAIN\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reco-Nova is a premium, enterprise-grade reconnaissance intelligence framework designed for professional security researchers, bug bounty hunters, and penetration testers. Built with modern Python 3.9+ and cutting-edge web technologies, it transforms raw reconnaissance data into actionable security intelligence.
.PP
The framework automates the entire reconnaissance lifecycle through 7 comprehensive phases:
.PP
.RS
1. Subdomain Discovery
.br
2. HTTP Probing & Endpoint Discovery
.br
3. URL & Parameter Discovery
.br
4. JavaScript Intelligence
.br
5. Sensitive Asset Detection
.br
6. Intelligence & Correlation
.br
7. Screenshots & Report Generation
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Target Options
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIDOMAIN\fR
Single target domain to scan (e.g., example.com)
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list " " \fIFILE\fR
File containing list of domains (one per line)
.SS Scan Options
.TP
.BR \-\-full
Run full reconnaissance with all modules enabled
.TP
.BR \-\-passive\-only
Use only passive sources (no active probing)
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-screenshots
Skip screenshot capture phase
.TP
.BR \-\-graph
Generate interactive attack surface graph (D3.js)
.SS Reporting Options
.TP
.BR \-\-simple
Generate classic/simple HTML report instead of modern Bootstrap theme
.TP
.BR \-\-output " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory (default: output)
.SS Performance Options
.TP
.BR \-\-threads " " \fIN\fR
Number of concurrent threads (default: 20)
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
HTTP request timeout in seconds (default: 15)
.SS Output Control
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable verbose debug output with detailed logging
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output mode
.SH COMMANDS
.SS setup
Verify and install all dependencies:
.PP
.B reco-nova setup
.PP
Checks for Python packages, Firefox, Go tools, and configures the environment.
.SS monitor
Enable continuous monitoring mode:
.PP
.B reco-nova monitor example.com --interval 3600
.PP
Monitors target for changes at specified interval (default: 3600 seconds).
.SS report
Generate final report for a previously scanned domain:
.PP
.B reco-nova report example.com
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic Scan
Scan a single domain with default settings:
.PP
.B reco-nova -d example.com
.SS Full Reconnaissance
Comprehensive scan with all features:
.PP
.B reco-nova -d example.com --full --graph
.SS Multiple Targets
Scan domains from a file:
.PP
.B reco-nova -l targets.txt --threads 30
.SS Passive Only
Passive reconnaissance without active probing:
.PP
.B reco-nova -d example.com --passive-only
.SS Classic Report
Generate simple HTML report instead of modern:
.PP
.B reco-nova -d example.com --simple
.SS Debug Mode
Enable detailed logging for troubleshooting:
.PP
.B reco-nova -d example.com --debug
.SH OUTPUT FILES
.SS Text Output (output/<domain>/)
.TP
.B subdomains.txt
All discovered subdomains
.TP
.B live_hosts.txt
Responsive HTTP hosts
.TP
.B urls.txt
Discovered URLs from all sources
.TP
.B parameters.txt
URL parameters grouped by name
.TP
.B apis.txt
API endpoints with status codes
.TP
.B secrets.txt
Potential credentials and tokens
.TP
.B sensitive_files.txt
Exposed sensitive files
.TP
.B cloud_assets.txt
Cloud storage assets (S3, Azure, GCP)
.SS Reports (reports/)
.TP
.B <domain>_modern.html
Modern Bootstrap dark theme report (default)
.TP
.B <domain>_report.html
Classic simple HTML report (--simple flag)
.SS Graphs (graphs/)
.TP
.B <domain>_graph.html
Interactive D3.js attack surface visualization
.TP
.B <domain>_graph.json
Machine-readable graph data
.SS Screenshots (output/<domain>/screenshots/)
.TP
.B *.png
Webpage screenshots captured with Firefox Headless
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution
.TP
.B 1
General error or scan failure
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or configuration
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHONPATH
Must include reco-nova directory for imports
.TP
.B PATH
Should include ~/.local/bin for Go tools
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.bashrc
Shell configuration with reco-nova alias
.TP
.B ~/.zshrc
Zsh configuration with reco-nova alias
.TP
.B /usr/local/bin/reco-nova
Global command symlink (after install)
.TP
.B /usr/share/man/man1/reco-nova.1.gz
Manual page location
.SH PHASES
Reco-Nova executes scans in 7 phases with professional terminal output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[Phase 1/7] [] Subdomain Discovery
[Phase 2/7] [~] HTTP Probing & Endpoint Discovery  
[Phase 3/7] [#] URL & Parameter Discovery
[Phase 4/7] {js} JavaScript Intelligence
[Phase 5/7] [!] Sensitive Asset Detection
[Phase 6/7] [f] Intelligence & Correlation
[Phase 7/7] [ss] Screenshots & Report
.fi
.RE
.SH ICONS
Professional terminal icons used throughout:
.TP
.B [*]
Informational message
.TP
.B [+]
Success/Completion
.TP
.B [!]
Warning/Alert
.TP
.B [-]
Error
.TP
.B [FOUND]
Discovery notification
.SH REPORTING
Two report formats are available:
.SS Modern Report (Default)
Generated as \fI<domain>_modern.html\fR:
.RS
- Bootstrap 5 dark theme
- Responsive design
- Screenshot gallery with lightbox
- Interactive statistics panels
- Professional color scheme
.RE
.SS Classic Report
Generated as \fI<domain>_report.html\fR with --simple flag:
.RS
- Simple HTML layout
- Minimal styling
- Fast rendering
- Portable format
.RE
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.SS Firefox Screenshots Not Working
Check Firefox installation:
.PP
.B firefox --version
.B firefox --headless --screenshot=/tmp/test.png https://example.com
.SS Permission Denied
Use passive-only mode or reduce threads:
.PP
.B reco-nova -d target.com --passive-only --threads 5
.SS Memory Issues
Process targets in batches:
.PP
.B reco-nova -l targets.txt --threads 10
.SS Debug Information
Enable debug logging:
.PP
.B reco-nova -d target.com --debug
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.SS Required
- Python 3.9+
- aiohttp
- beautifulsoup4
- rich
.SS Optional (Enhanced Features)
- Firefox (screenshots)
- subfinder (subdomain discovery)
- httpx (HTTP probing)
- amass (subdomain enumeration)
- gowitness (screenshot fallback)
